{
  "source": "course-assets/avoid-traps-opener/avoid-traps-opener.mp4",
  "duration": 215.2746875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 12.34,
      "text": "The false fact sounds sure, the flattery feels good, the fake looks real, this is the baseline rule of our course, every trap looks completely fine from the inside."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.28,
      "end": 20.86,
      "text": "The exact same machinery that makes artificial intelligence so capable also causes it to fail in specific predictable ways."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.66,
      "end": 27.72,
      "text": "With traditional software, errors are obvious, we instinctively look for typos or disjointed syntax,"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.72,
      "end": 34.52,
      "text": "but AI doesn't glitch, it delivers mistakes wrapped in a clean, grammatically perfect sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.24,
      "end": 42.22,
      "text": "You're looking at a flawless structure, but the fact inside is entirely made up, it reads exactly like a real one."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.86,
      "end": 49.12,
      "text": "Because AI errors bypass our standard internal alarms, relying on gut instinct will leave you exposed."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.88,
      "end": 53.84,
      "text": "We have to build an entirely new mental model to navigate these tools safely."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.84,
      "end": 61.88,
      "text": "Think about a rip current in the ocean, it doesn't look dangerous, to most people it looks like the safest best spot on the beach,"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.3,
      "end": 65.56,
      "text": "a calm, flat channel cutting right between the breaking waves."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.3,
      "end": 72.8,
      "text": "Swim into that inviting calm water, and you will be pulled straight out far from the shore."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.5,
      "end": 81.66,
      "text": "Survival in this situation does not depend on out swimming the current once it has you, it depends on spotting it before you get your feet wet."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.28,
      "end": 91.9,
      "text": "Lifeguards identify these traps all day long. They aren't superhuman swimmers, they simply recognize the exact shape a rip current makes in the water."
    },
    {
      "start": 92.62,
      "end": 99.98,
      "text": "AI systems have their own rip currents, and just like the ocean, the most dangerous areas often look the most helpful and inviting."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.8,
      "end": 106.26,
      "text": "A rip current is not the ocean malfunctioning, it is just water following the physics of the shoreline."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.26,
      "end": 110.6,
      "text": "Every AI trap we will cover operates the exact same way."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.24,
      "end": 115.06,
      "text": "These are not glitches, they are the models functioning exactly as designed."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.8,
      "end": 123.98,
      "text": "Our goal here is to train your eye. By learning the distinct patterns these dangers form, you can avoid the current entirely, instead of fighting it."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.54,
      "end": 130.06,
      "text": "This roadmap shows what we'll explore in this section. The first category is traps and the answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.06,
      "end": 133.6,
      "text": "This covers the ways a model's output goes wrong internally."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.28,
      "end": 142.02,
      "text": "These mechanisms include entirely invented facts, hidden biases built into the training data, and stale knowledge from outdated information."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.9,
      "end": 148.98,
      "text": "It also includes the dangerous habit these models have of confidently summarizing documents they never actually read."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.82,
      "end": 156.34,
      "text": "Next are traps in you. Most people do not consider their own psychology of vulnerability when evaluating software,"
    },
    {
      "start": 156.34,
      "end": 161.74,
      "text": "but these models are explicitly designed to be helpful, agreeable, and engaging."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.54,
      "end": 169.96,
      "text": "That design actively works on your natural human responses, making the AI easy to use, and very easy to fall for."
    },
    {
      "start": 170.54,
      "end": 176.96,
      "text": "The final category is traps from the world. This is the external threat, the trap that comes looking for you."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.42,
      "end": 181.34,
      "text": "Other people can weaponize these same systems to put deepfakes in front of you."
    },
    {
      "start": 181.34,
      "end": 188.2,
      "text": "They can generate media that is so convincing, seeing it with your own eyes is no longer proof of reality."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.06,
      "end": 195.98,
      "text": "Having this three-part map is your foundation. Once you know where to look, you can see these structures forming in real time."
    },
    {
      "start": 196.76,
      "end": 207.54,
      "text": "Recognizing the pattern is the real skill. Our greatest vulnerability with artificial intelligence is the assumption that errors will announce themselves, when AI fails, nothing looks broken."
    },
    {
      "start": 208.3,
      "end": 210.96,
      "text": "This section teaches you to read the water."
    }
  ],
